GRAMMAR.md §3.1 rule 2, TYPES.md §2 (log-2026-09-28 "check follow-ups 4 review", "round 3"): "??"
never ends a line, so a field's "T??" directly followed by another field on the next line is one
mistake (E3401), not also a missing separator (E1117, syntax owns the fix).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

record R {
  a: Int??
  b: Int
}
-- findings.txt --
warning[W1002]  a/a.canon:3:8
  record R has no doc comment

warning[W1002]  a/a.canon:4:3
  field a has no doc comment

error[E3401]  a/a.canon:4:6
  Int?? is not a type: Int? is already optional

warning[W1002]  a/a.canon:5:3
  field b has no doc comment

1 error, 3 warnings in 1 package (…)
